.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Raw source snapshots are fetched, not committed (see docs/provenance.md).
# Raw upstream sources.
#
# The small ones are committed. They total ~756 KB, and after the os-climate bucket
# was disabled on 2026-08-12 there is real value in the inputs being inspectable and
# diffable in the repository itself rather than only reachable through a download.
#
# Two things stay out:
#   - HazusWindDamFunctions_Hazus61.xlsx (97.4 MiB). Git history is permanent, and
#     committing it would roughly double the cost of every clone and every
#     `pip install git+...` forever. It is a v0.1.0 release asset instead, and
#     fetch.py pulls it from there with SHA-256 verification.
#   - FEMA PDFs (~35 MB). FEMA's to distribute, and fetch.py --docs retrieves them.
raw/*
!raw/MANIFEST.json
!raw/*.csv
!raw/HazusFloodDamageFunctions_Hazus61.xlsx

# Build artifacts ship as GitHub Release assets, not in git.
dist/

.DS_Store
site/data/
